\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone 
\par 1. O LOVE Divine! Whose 
\par constant beam
\par Shines on the eyes that will not see,
\par And waits to bless us, while we dream
\par Thou leav'st us when we turn from 
\par Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. All souls that struggle and aspire,
\par All hearts of prayer, by Thee are lit;
\par And, dim or clear, Thy tongues of fire
\par On dusky tribes and centuries sit.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Nor bounds nor clime nor creed 
\par Thou know'st
\par Wide as our need Thy favours fall;
\par The white wings of the Holy ghost
\par Stoop unseen o'er the heads of all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Truth, which the sage and prophet 
\par saw,
\par Long sought without, but found within,
\par The law of love beyond all law,
\par The life o'erflooding death and sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Shine, the light of God! Make 
\par broad Thy scope
\par To all who sin and suffer; more
\par And better than we dare to hope
\par Make with thy love our longings poor.
\par                                      AMEN\lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\f2\fs16 
\par }

